From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SplitPlay <splitplay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] splitplay: product identity for splitplay-worker

Turn the Sunshine executable into the SplitPlay desk worker:

- The executable is named splitplay-worker (OUTPUT_NAME; the CMake target
  keeps its upstream name so the rest of the build is untouched), and the
  Windows version resource names it.
- SPLITPLAY_VERSION and SPLITPLAY_UPSTREAM_COMMIT cache variables feed a
  version string ("splitplay-worker 0.1.0 (SplitPlay desk worker, based on
  Sunshine cf52f4b6)") printed by --version before anything touches the
  disk, at the top of --help and in the log.
- New option --desk-dir <dir> (also --desk-dir=<dir>): platf::appdata()
  returns it on Windows, so sunshine.conf, sunshine_state.json,
  credentials/, apps.json, covers/ and sunshine.log all live in the
  per-desk directory that SplitPlay.Service passes. The options are read
  from GetCommandLineW() because the upstream config defaults call
  appdata() during static initialisation, and they are removed from argv
  before the upstream parser sees them.
- The working directory is set to the executable's directory so that the
  relative assets path resolves wherever the service starts the worker.
- The tray icon is off by default (SUNSHINE_ENABLE_TRAY=OFF), and
  launch_ui() only logs the URL instead of opening a browser.

